---
layout: base.njk
title: Research & Projects
permalink: /research/
---

<header class="wrap page-head">
  <h1 class="page-head__title">Research &amp; Projects</h1>
  <p class="page-head__lede">
    Longer work that does not fit an article: student research, data projects, long-form reports,
    economic models, policy papers and surveys.
  </p>
</header>

{% if collections.projects.length %}
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="stack">
      {% for project in collections.projects %}
        <article class="row reveal">
          <a class="row__link" href="{{ project.url }}">
            <div class="row__media">
              <img src="{{ project.data.image or '/images/abstract-research.svg' }}" alt="" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="row__body">
              <p class="label">{{ project.data.kind }}{% if project.data.status %} · {{ project.data.status }}{% endif %}</p>
              <h2 class="row__title">{{ project.data.title }}</h2>
              <p class="row__subtitle">{{ project.data.subtitle }}</p>
              <p class="meta">
                {% set lead = project.data.author | author %}
                <span class="meta__author">{{ lead.name if lead else project.data.author }}</span>
                <span class="meta__dot">·</span>
                {{ project.date | monthYear }}
              </p>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
{% else %}
  <section class="wrap">
    <p class="empty">No projects published yet.</p>
  </section>
{% endif %}

<section class="wrap prose prose--page">
  <h2>Proposing a project</h2>
  <p>
    Research projects can be collaborative and can run over a term or longer. If you have a
    dissertation, dataset or model you think deserves a wider readership, tell us about it.
  </p>
</section>
